# Documentation Governance

Documentation is a **first-class system component**, not an afterthought.

## Single Source of Truth (Strict)

Each concept must live in **exactly one place**.

Other documents may:

- Link to it
- Briefly reference it

They must NOT:

- Re-explain it
- Duplicate steps, tables, or lists

Duplication is considered a defect.

---

## Canonical Ownership

| Topic | Canonical File |
| ---- | ---- |
| Quick onboarding | QUICK_START.md |
| Full setup | SETUP_GUIDE.md |
| Commands & usage | COMMANDS.md |
| Web UI | WEB_DASHBOARD_GUIDE.md |
| API behavior | API_GUIDE.md |
| Architecture | design/ARCHITECTURE.md |
| Roadmap | roadmap/ROADMAP.md |
| Change history | CHANGELOG.md |
| Troubleshooting | TROUBLESHOOTING.md |

If content belongs in one of these, do not place it elsewhere.

---

## Documentation Refactors

When asked to clean or improve docs:

You MUST:

1. Identify duplicated or overlapping content
2. Choose a canonical location
3. Remove duplicates
4. Replace them with hyperlinks
5. Verify `INDEX.md` navigation accuracy
6. Identify redundant docs and docs that are no longer applicable or needed

Explicitly call out what was removed and why.

---

## Documentation Tone

- Precise, not verbose
- Actionable, not theoretical
- Structured with headings, tables, and links
